     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Disimpaction may need oral, oral then rectal, or rectal then oral tx; some children need only laxatives (no enemas or suppositories). Often used: PEG w electrolytes (± a stimulant laxative, eg, bisacodyl, senna), or saline enemas + a 2-wk regimen of oral agents and suppositories. Maintenance: PEG without electrolytes is used most often, titrated to 1 to 2 semisoft stools a day; then slow withdrawal of laxatives once Sx resolve. Glycerin suppository, infants and children < 2 y: 1/2–1 pediatric suppository once/day for up to 3 days."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
